<!-- Animal Redux: this mod's own GUI profiles.

     AR HAS NEVER HAD ONE UNTIL NOW. Every profile its layouts name is either the
     base game's or one of DR's (SDList, SDRowCell, SDHeaderLeft, SDBarLabel,
     SDInputsDialogBox), which is a dependency worth being aware of but is not
     what this file is for. It exists for the TEXT PICKER, whose two pieces have
     no stock equivalent.

     BOTH ARE ANCHORED, NOT POSITIONED. DR 5.70 records a text input and its label
     ignoring an absolute x/y outright, because a stock profile places itself; and
     DR 5.87a records that "with" is read on PROFILES ONLY and is silently ignored
     on an element. So the anchoring lives here, where it is actually read.

     THE 80px INSET IS THE TWO ARROWS. fs25_multiTextOptionLeft and Right are 40px
     each and anchor to the ends of their container, so 40 off each side leaves the
     middle to the field. It is DELIBERATELY WIDER THAN THE STOCK TEXT PROFILE'S
     50px total: a text input CONSUMES a mouse click where a text label does not,
     so any overlap with an arrow would be a dead arrow.

     COMMENT RULE: no double hyphen inside an XML comment. It is a parse error and
     FS25 answers it by not loading the layout at all; DR records it costing six
     builds. tools/check_xml.py catches it before a deploy. -->
<GUIProfiles>

    <!-- THE FIELD. Transparent by inheritance: fs25_textInput sets imageSliceId
         noSlice and every image colour to zero, so the multiTextOption background
         behind it shows through and the control looks exactly like the selector it
         replaces. maxInputTextWidth is cut to the 260px this actually occupies
         (340 box less the two 40px arrows), from the 229 the stock profile sizes
         for its own 249px box. -->
    <Profile name="ARNumberInput" extends="fs25_textInput" with="anchorStretchingYStretchingX">
        <size value="100% 100%" />
        <absoluteSizeOffset value="80px 0px" />

        <textSize value="16px" />
        <textAlignment value="center" />
        <textColor value="0.9 0.9 0.9 1" />
        <maxInputTextWidth value="240px" />
    </Profile>

    <!-- THE GREY PROMPT that sits over the field while it is empty. A SEPARATE
         ELEMENT because TextInputElement has no placeholder at all (imePlaceholder
         reaches the console IME overlay and never the field), and because a prompt
         held in the field's own text becomes real input the moment a character is
         appended to it.

         It cannot steal the click: TextElement declares no mouseEvent of its own
         and GuiElement:mouseEvent only propagates. Read in the shipped source,
         not assumed, because a prompt that ate the click would make the field
         unfocusable and read as a dead control.

         SMALLER AND DIMMER THAN THE VALUE, so a prompt is never mistaken for a
         number that has been chosen. The value is 16px at 0.9 grey. -->
    <Profile name="ARNumberHint" extends="fs25_textDefault" with="anchorStretchingYStretchingX">
        <size value="100% 100%" />
        <absoluteSizeOffset value="80px 0px" />

        <textSize value="14px" />
        <textAlignment value="center" />
        <textColor value="0.5 0.5 0.5 1" />
        <textMaxNumLines value="1" />
    </Profile>


    <!-- THE BASE GAME'S OWN ON / OFF SWITCH, the one the Game Settings screen uses
         for Traffic and Snow. Requested 2026-09-02 in place of a two entry
         selector ring: a ring makes a yes/no answer look like a list you step
         through, and both states are visible at once on a real switch.

         BinaryOptionElement EXTENDS MultiTextOptionElement, so it answers setTexts,
         setState, getState and raises onClick exactly the same way. That is what
         makes this a swap of the element rather than of the handler.

         EVERY PART OF IT IS PERCENTAGE SIZED (the two halves are 50% 100%, the
         background and slider stretch), so it scales to whatever box it is put in.
         Stretched to fill the 340px slot so it lines up with the typed fields
         above and below it rather than sitting narrower in the middle. -->
    <Profile name="ARToggle" extends="fs25_binaryOption" with="anchorStretchingYStretchingX">
        <size value="100% 100%" />
    </Profile>


    <!-- AN IN-ROW ARROW. DR 5.64 proved a Button can live inside a SmoothList row
         and be clicked: SmoothListElement:mouseEvent calls its SUPERCLASS FIRST and
         gates its own row selection on "not eventUsed", so a child that consumes a
         click fires AND the row does not also select.

         THE ANCHOR IS THE ONLY OVERRIDE, per that entry's hard-won rule: resize the
         stock arrow and it samples the UI atlas wrongly and renders as garbled
         blocks. fs25_multiTextOptionRight anchors to its PARENT's right edge, which
         in a row is the far end of the row rather than the end of its cell, so it is
         re-anchored LEFT and then placed by position like everything else. The left
         arrow needs no profile at all: the stock one is already left anchored.

         AR's OWN rather than DR's SDRowArrowRight, which is identical: this mod
         already leans on DR for a dozen profiles and there is no reason to add a
         thirteenth for one line. -->
    <Profile name="ARRowArrowRight" extends="fs25_multiTextOptionRight" with="anchorStretchingYLeft" />

</GUIProfiles>
